This n8n workflow creates a simple **mobile app / Telegram AI assistant** that can handle both text messages and images. It starts when a user sends a message to your Telegram bot (or through the webhook),
then a Switch node checks whether the message contains normal text or a photo. If it’s a text message, the workflow saves the text and sends it directly to an AI Agent. If it’s an image, it first downloads
the image, then uses an OpenAI Vision model (GPT-4o-mini) to analyze the image and generate a detailed description (including objects, environment, and any text inside the image). That image analysis is
then combined with the user’s message and passed into an AI Agent powered by Groq (Llama 3.1 8B) with a memory window of the last 10 messages, so the bot can reply in a conversational way. Finally, the
assistant sends the final AI response back to the user on Telegram, making it a complete chat + vision assistant that works like a lightweight mobile support bot. 
